{"type":"message","id":"cd584c91","parentId":"03cc14d1","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:07:51.989Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-04 12:07 GMT+8] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 2/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: ## Task: Fix High Priority Issues (H1, H2, H3)\n\n## Workspace: /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor\n\n## Context\nPixelArtEditor project has 3 high priority bugs that need immediate fixing.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### H1: Add destroy() method (Memory Leak)\n**File:** `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts`\n\nAdd a `destroy()` method to clean up event listeners:\n```typescript\ndestroy(): void {\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n  this.#listeners = [];\n}\n```\n\n### H2: RGB Value Range Validation\n**File:** `src/crdt/PixelData.ts`\n\nIn the `set` method, add RGB value validation:\n```typescript\nif (value[0] < 0 || value[0] > 255 || \n    value[1] < 0 || value[1] > 255 || \n    value[2] < 0 || value[2] > 255) {\n  throw new RangeError(`RGB values must be 0-255, got [${value}]`);\n}\n```\n\n### H3: Binary Decoder Boundary Check\n**File:** `src/encoding/Decoder.ts`\n\nAdd chunk length overflow check to prevent buffer overruns.\n\n## Deliverable\n- All 3 fixes implemented and working\n- Run `npm test` to verify no regressions\n- Brief report of changes made\n\n## Report To: $HOME/.openclaw-reports/code-agent/"}],"timestamp":1772597271986}}
{"type":"message","id":"102dcb63","parentId":"cd584c91","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:08:03.236Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to fix 3 high priority issues in the PixelArtEditor project. Let me start by reading the relevant files to understand the current state and then implement the fixes.\n\nLet me read the three files mentioned:\n1. `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts` - for H1 (destroy method)\n2. `src/crdt/PixelData.ts` - for H2 (RGB validation)\n3. `src/encoding/Decoder.ts` - for H3 (boundary check)","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll fix these 3 high priority bugs. Let me start by reading the current files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-afe641e9972d421ab48bf895f7f91aa0","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/editor/PixelEditor.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-9298c75b85354a909f36d446e0f801fe","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/crdt/PixelData.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-26015b7766424c6f80948b615f1cd004","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/encoding/Decoder.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":9044,"output":290,"cacheRead":3423,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12757,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772597271988}}
{"type":"message","id":"33593a75","parentId":"102dcb63","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:08:03.242Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-afe641e9972d421ab48bf895f7f91aa0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { RGB, PixelDataState, ArtboardSize } from \"../types.js\";\nimport { PixelData } from \"../crdt/PixelData.js\";\nimport { Encoder } from \"../encoding/Encoder.js\";\nimport { Decoder } from \"../encoding/Decoder.js\";\n\n/**\n * Compression mode\n */\nexport type CompressionMode = \"none\" | \"binary\";\n\n/**\n * PixelEditor - Canvas-based pixel art editor with CRDT sync\n */\nexport class PixelEditor {\n  /** The underlying canvas element */\n  #el: HTMLCanvasElement;\n\n  /** 2D canvas rendering context */\n  #ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D;\n\n  /** Artboard size in drawable pixels */\n  #artboard: ArtboardSize;\n\n  /** Underlying pixel data CRDT */\n  #data: PixelData;\n\n  /** Selected drawing color */\n  #color: RGB = [0, 0, 0];\n\n  /** Previous cursor position for line drawing */\n  #prev: [x: number, y: number] | undefined;\n\n  /** Painted pixels during current drag (for timestamp optimization) */\n  #painted = new Set<string>();\n\n  /** Change event listeners */\n  #listeners: Array<(data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array) => void> = [];\n\n  /** Compression mode */\n  #compressionMode: CompressionMode = \"none\";\n\n  /** Encoder instance */\n  #encoder?: Encoder;\n\n  /** Decoder instance */\n  #decoder?: Decoder;\n\n  /**\n   * Set the compression mode\n   */\n  set compressionMode(mode: CompressionMode) {\n    this.#compressionMode = mode;\n    if (mode === \"binary\") {\n      this.#encoder = new Encoder(this.#artboard.w, this.#artboard.h);\n      this.#decoder = new Decoder();\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the compression mode\n   */\n  get compressionMode(): CompressionMode {\n    return this.#compressionMode;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set the drawing color\n   */\n  set color(color: RGB) {\n    this.#color = color;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the drawing color\n   */\n  get color(): RGB {\n    return this.#color;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Create a new PixelEditor\n   * @param el - Canvas element\n   * @param artboard - Artboard dimensions\n   * @param id - Unique peer ID (optional, generates UUID if not provided)\n   */\n  constructor(el: HTMLCanvasElement, artboard: ArtboardSize, id?: string) {\n    this.#el = el;\n    this.#artboard = artboard;\n\n    const ctx = el.getContext(\"2d\");\n    if (!ctx) throw new Error(\"Couldn't get 2D rendering context\");\n    this.#ctx = ctx;\n\n    this.#data = new PixelData(id ?? crypto.randomUUID());\n\n    // Listen for pointer events\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n\n    // Handle high-DPI displays\n    this.#el.width = this.#el.clientWidth * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#el.height = this.#el.clientHeight * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#ctx.scale(devicePixelRatio, devicePixelRatio);\n    this.#ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;\n\n    // Initial draw\n    this.#draw();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Add a change listener\n   */\n  set onchange(listener: (data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array) => void) {\n    this.#listeners.push(listener);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Handle pointer events (implements EventListener interface)\n   */\n  handleEvent(e: PointerEvent): void {\n    switch (e.type) {\n      case \"pointerdown\": {\n        this.#el.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n        // Clear painted set for new drag\n        this.#painted.clear();\n        // Fall through to paint\n      }\n      // eslint-disable-next-line no-fallthrough\n      case \"pointermove\": {\n        if (!this.#el.hasPointerCapture(e.pointerId)) return;\n\n        // Convert canvas pixels to artboard pixels\n        const x = Math.floor(\n          (this.#artboard.w * e.offsetX) / this.#el.clientWidth\n        );\n        const y = Math.floor(\n          (this.#artboard.h * e.offsetY) / this.#el.clientHeight\n        );\n\n        this.#paint(x, y);\n        this.#prev = [x, y];\n        break;\n      }\n      case \"pointerup\": {\n        this.#el.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n        this.#prev = undefined;\n        this.#painted.clear();\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Paint a pixel and draw a line from previous position\n   */\n  #paint(x: number, y: number): void {\n    // Bounds check\n    if (x < 0 || this.#artboard.w <= x) return;\n    if (y < 0 || this.#artboard.h <= y) return;\n\n    // Timestamp optimization: skip if already painted in this drag\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    if (this.#painted.has(key)) return;\n    this.#painted.add(key);\n\n    // Set the pixel\n    this.#data.set(x, y, this.#color);\n\n    // Draw line from previous position using DDA algorithm\n    if (this.#prev) {\n      const [px, py] = this.#prev;\n      this.#drawLine(px, py, x, y);\n    }\n\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#notify();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw a line between two points using DDA algorithm\n   */\n  #drawLine(x0: number, y0: number, x1: number, y1: number): void {\n    const dx = x1 - x0;\n    const dy = y1 - y0;\n    const steps = Math.max(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));\n\n    if (steps === 0) return;\n\n    const xInc = dx / steps;\n    const yInc = dy / steps;\n\n    let x = x0;\n    let y = y0;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\n      x += xInc;\n      y += yInc;\n      const ix = Math.round(x);\n      const iy = Math.round(y);\n\n      // Bounds check\n      if (ix < 0 || this.#artboard.w <= ix) continue;\n      if (iy < 0 || this.#artboard.h <= iy) continue;\n\n      // Timestamp optimization\n      const key = PixelData.key(ix, iy);\n      if (this.#painted.has(key)) continue;\n      this.#painted.add(key);\n\n      this.#data.set(ix, iy, this.#color);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw all pixels to canvas\n   */\n  async #draw(): Promise<void> {\n    const chans = 4; // RGBA\n    const buffer = new Uint8ClampedArray(\n      this.#artboard.w * this.#artboard.h * chans\n    );\n    const rowsize = this.#artboard.w * chans;\n\n    for (let row = 0; row < this.#artboard.h; row++) {\n      const offsetY = row * rowsize;\n      for (let col = 0; col < this.#artboard.w; col++) {\n        const offsetX = col * chans;\n        const offset = offsetY + offsetX;\n\n        const [r, g, b] = this.#data.get(col, row);\n        buffer[offset] = r;\n        buffer[offset + 1] = g;\n        buffer[offset + 2] = b;\n        buffer[offset + 3] = 255; // Alpha\n      }\n    }\n\n    const data = new ImageData(buffer, this.#artboard.w, this.#artboard.h);\n    const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(data);\n    this.#ctx.drawImage(\n      bitmap,\n      0,\n      0,\n      this.#el.clientWidth,\n      this.#el.clientHeight\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Notify listeners of state change\n   */\n  #notify(): void {\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n\n    if (this.#compressionMode === \"binary\" && this.#encoder) {\n      const encoded = this.#encoder.encode(state);\n      for (const listener of this.#listeners) {\n        listener(encoded);\n      }\n    } else {\n      for (const listener of this.#listeners) {\n        listener(state);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Receive and merge remote state\n   */\n  receive(data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array): void {\n    if (this.#compressionMode === \"binary\" && this.#decoder && data instanceof Uint8Array) {\n      const { state } = this.#decoder.decode(data);\n      this.#data.merge(state);\n    } else if (data instanceof Uint8Array) {\n      throw new Error(\"Received binary data but binary mode is not enabled\");\n    } else {\n      this.#data.merge(data);\n    }\n    this.#draw();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the current state\n   */\n  get state(): PixelDataState {\n    return this.#data.state;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the current artboard size\n   */\n  get artboard(): ArtboardSize {\n    return { ...this.#artboard };\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772597283241}}
{"type":"message","id":"116cb6db","parentId":"33593a75","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:08:03.247Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-9298c75b85354a909f36d446e0f801fe","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { RGB, PixelDataState } from \"../types.js\";\nimport { LWWMap } from \"./LWWMap.js\";\n\n/**\n * PixelData - Thin wrapper over LWWMap for pixel coordinates\n * \n * Maps (x, y) coordinates to RGB colors using an underlying LWW Map.\n * Default color is white [255, 255, 255].\n */\nexport class PixelData {\n  /** Unique peer ID */\n  readonly id: string;\n  \n  /** Underlying LWW Map */\n  #data: LWWMap<RGB>;\n\n  /**\n   * Get the current value (map of \"x,y\" -> RGB)\n   */\n  get value(): Record<string, RGB> {\n    return this.#data.value;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the full state for serialization\n   */\n  get state(): PixelDataState {\n    return this.#data.state;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Create a new PixelData instance\n   * @param id - Unique peer ID\n   * @param state - Optional initial state\n   */\n  constructor(id: string, state?: PixelDataState) {\n    this.id = id;\n    this.#data = new LWWMap(this.id, state ?? {});\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Generate a string key from coordinates\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   * @returns String key \"x,y\"\n   */\n  static key(x: number, y: number): string {\n    return `${x},${y}`;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set a pixel color\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   * @param value - RGB color\n   */\n  set(x: number, y: number, value: RGB): void {\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    this.#data.set(key, value);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get a pixel color\n   * Returns white [255, 255, 255] if not set\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   * @returns RGB color\n   */\n  get(x: number, y: number): RGB {\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    const value = this.#data.get(key);\n    return value ?? [255, 255, 255];\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Delete a pixel (set to tombstone)\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   */\n  delete(x: number, y: number): void {\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    this.#data.delete(key);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Merge remote state\n   * @param state - Remote state to merge\n   */\n  merge(state: PixelDataState): void {\n    this.#data.merge(state);\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772597283246}}
{"type":"message","id":"5006660f","parentId":"116cb6db","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:08:03.253Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-26015b7766424c6f80948b615f1cd004","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { PixelDataState, RGB } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/**\n * Decoder - Converts binary format to PixelData state\n */\nexport class Decoder {\n  #width = 0;\n  #height = 0;\n  #uuidTable: string[] = [];\n  #paletteTable: RGB[] = [];\n\n  /**\n   * Decode binary data to state\n   */\n  decode(data: Uint8Array): { state: PixelDataState; width: number; height: number } {\n    let offset = 0;\n\n    // Read magic number\n    const magic = String.fromCharCode(\n      data[offset],\n      data[offset + 1],\n      data[offset + 2],\n      data[offset + 3]\n    );\n    if (magic !== \"CRDT\") {\n      throw new Error(\"Invalid magic number\");\n    }\n    offset += 4;\n\n    // Read width and height\n    const view = new DataView(data.buffer, data.byteOffset, data.length);\n    this.#width = view.getUint16(offset);\n    this.#height = view.getUint16(offset + 2);\n    offset += 4;\n\n    // Read chunks\n    while (offset < data.length) {\n      const chunkId = String.fromCharCode(\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n        data[offset + 3]\n      );\n      const chunkLength = view.getUint16(offset + 4);\n      offset += 6;\n\n      const chunkData = data.slice(offset, offset + chunkLength);\n      offset += chunkLength;\n\n      switch (chunkId) {\n        case \"UUID\":\n          this.#decodeUUIDChunk(chunkData);\n          break;\n        case \"PLTT\":\n          this.#decodePaletteChunk(chunkData);\n          break;\n        case \"DATA\":\n          return {\n            state: this.#decodeDataChunk(chunkData),\n            width: this.#width,\n            height: this.#height,\n          };\n        default:\n          throw new Error(`Unknown chunk: ${chunkId}`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    throw new Error(\"Missing DATA chunk\");\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode UUID chunk\n   */\n  #decodeUUIDChunk(data: Uint8Array): void {\n    const uuidCount = data.length / 16;\n    this.#uuidTable = [];\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < uuidCount; i++) {\n      const offset = i * 16;\n      let hex = \"\";\n      for (let j = 0; j < 16; j++) {\n        hex += data[offset + j].toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\");\n      }\n      // Add hyphens back\n      const uuid = [\n        hex.substring(0, 8),\n        hex.substring(8, 12),\n        hex.substring(12, 16),\n        hex.substring(16, 20),\n        hex.substring(20),\n      ].join(\"-\");\n      this.#uuidTable.push(uuid);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode palette chunk\n   * Note: First 3 bytes are dummy (index 0 reserved for erased pixels)\n   */\n  #decodePaletteChunk(data: Uint8Array): void {\n    // Skip first 3 bytes (dummy at index 0)\n    const colorCount = (data.length - 3) / 3;\n    this.#paletteTable = [null as unknown as RGB]; // index 0 = null/erased\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < colorCount; i++) {\n      const offset = 3 + i * 3; // Skip first 3 bytes\n      this.#paletteTable.push([\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n      ]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode data chunk\n   */\n  #decodeDataChunk(data: Uint8Array): PixelDataState {\n    const state: PixelDataState = {};\n    let offset = 0;\n    let x = 0;\n    let y = 0;\n    const view = new DataView(data.buffer, data.byteOffset, data.length);\n\n    while (y < this.#height && offset < data.length) {\n      const tag = data[offset];\n\n      if (tag === TAG_BLANK) {\n        // Blank run\n        const count = view.getUint16(offset + 1);\n        offset += 3;\n\n        // Skip blank pixels\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n          x++;\n          if (x >= this.#width) {\n            x = 0;\n            y++;\n          }\n        }\n      } else if (tag === TAG_PIXEL) {\n        // Pixel\n        const writerId = data[offset + 1];\n        const timestamp = data[offset + 2];\n        const colorId = data[offset + 3];\n        offset += 4;\n\n        const key = `${x},${y}`;\n        const peerId = this.#uuidTable[writerId];\n        const color = colorId === 0 ? null : this.#paletteTable[colorId];\n\n        state[key] = [peerId, timestamp, color];\n\n        x++;\n        if (x >= this.#width) {\n          x = 0;\n          y++;\n        }\n      } else {\n        throw new Error(`Invalid tag: ${tag}`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    return state;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set height (deprecated, now read from INFO chunk)\n   */\n  setHeight(height: number): void {\n    this.#height = height;\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Data item types in run-length encoding\n */\nconst TAG_BLANK = 0;\nconst TAG_PIXEL = 1;"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772597283252}}
{"type":"message","id":"c7c7de3a","parentId":"5006660f","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:08:22.326Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all three files. Let me implement the fixes:\n\n1. **H1 - PixelEditor.ts**: Add a `destroy()` method to clean up event listeners. The spec shows:\n```typescript\ndestroy(): void {\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n  this.#listeners = [];\n}\n```\n\n2. **H2 - PixelData.ts**: Add RGB validation in the `set` method. The spec shows:\n```typescript\nif (value[0] < 0 || value[0] > 255 || \n    value[1] < 0 || value[1] > 255 || \n    value[2] < 0 || value[2] > 255) {\n  throw new RangeError(`RGB values must be 0-255, got [${value}]`);\n}\n```\n\n3. **H3 - Decoder.ts**: Add chunk length overflow check. Looking at the code, in the `decode` method, after reading `chunkLength`, we should check that `offset + chunkLength` doesn't exceed `data.length` to prevent buffer overruns.\n\nLet me make these edits.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll implement all three fixes:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-57325dd6ee7343368464cbc247ae6fe7","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/editor/PixelEditor.ts","newText":"/**\n   * Get the current artboard size\n   */\n  get artboard(): ArtboardSize {\n    return { ...this.#artboard };\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Clean up event listeners and resources\n   */\n  destroy(): void {\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n    this.#listeners = [];\n  }\n}","oldText":"/**\n   * Get the current artboard size\n   */\n  get artboard(): ArtboardSize {\n    return { ...this.#artboard };\n  }\n}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-a99a765aff354a788d5ad0709cd28e15","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/crdt/PixelData.ts","newText":"/**\n   * Set a pixel color\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   * @param value - RGB color\n   */\n  set(x: number, y: number, value: RGB): void {\n    if (value[0] < 0 || value[0] > 255 ||\n        value[1] < 0 || value[1] > 255 ||\n        value[2] < 0 || value[2] > 255) {\n      throw new RangeError(`RGB values must be 0-255, got [${value}]`);\n    }\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    this.#data.set(key, value);\n  }","oldText":"/**\n   * Set a pixel color\n   * @param x - X coordinate\n   * @param y - Y coordinate\n   * @param value - RGB color\n   */\n  set(x: number, y: number, value: RGB): void {\n    const key = PixelData.key(x, y);\n    this.#data.set(key, value);\n  }"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-0786f7feddd241d89caa98fc041e44df","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/encoding/Decoder.ts","newText":"const chunkId = String.fromCharCode(\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n        data[offset + 3]\n      );\n      const chunkLength = view.getUint16(offset + 4);\n      offset += 6;\n\n      // Boundary check: prevent buffer overrun\n      if (offset + chunkLength > data.length) {\n        throw new Error(`Chunk ${chunkId} overflows buffer: offset=${offset}, length=${chunkLength}, buffer=${data.length}`);\n      }\n\n      const chunkData = data.slice(offset, offset + chunkLength);","oldText":"const chunkId = String.fromCharCode(\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n        data[offset + 3]\n      );\n      const chunkLength = view.getUint16(offset + 4);\n      offset += 6;\n\n      const chunkData = data.slice(offset, offset + chunkLength);"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":3812,"output":1174,"cacheRead":12465,"cacheWrite":0,"totalToken